{"code":"47-2073.00","title":"Operating Engineers and Other Construction Equipment Operators","description":"Operate one or several types of power construction equipment, such as motor graders, bulldozers, scrapers, compressors, pumps, derricks, shovels, tractors, or front-end loaders to excavate, move, and grade earth, erect structures, or pour concrete or other hard surface pavement. May repair and maintain equipment in addition to other duties.","jobZone":2,"kinds":{"R":{"score":7,"share":0.5352},"I":{"score":2.93,"share":0.1722},"A":{"score":1,"share":0},"S":{"score":1.14,"share":0.0125},"E":{"score":1.26,"share":0.0232},"C":{"score":3.88,"share":0.2569}},"highPoints":["R","C","I"],"tasks":[{"id":9849,"text":"Learn and follow safety regulations.","core":true,"importance":4.86,"relevance":99.71,"frequency":5.87},{"id":9850,"text":"Take actions to avoid potential hazards or obstructions, such as utility lines, other equipment, other workers, or falling objects.","core":true,"importance":4.68,"relevance":88.58,"frequency":5.52},{"id":9861,"text":"Check fuel supplies at sites to ensure adequate availability.","core":false,"importance":4.67,"relevance":63.13,"frequency":4.78},{"id":9852,"text":"Start engines, move throttles, switches, or levers, or depress pedals to operate machines, such as bulldozers, trench excavators, road graders, or backhoes.","core":true,"importance":4.59,"relevance":93.75,"frequency":6.02},{"id":9858,"text":"Coordinate machine actions with other activities, positioning or moving loads in response to hand or audio signals from crew members.","core":true,"importance":4.53,"relevance":87.03,"frequency":4.85},{"id":9853,"text":"Locate underground services, such as pipes or wires, prior to beginning work.","core":true,"importance":4.48,"relevance":85.01,"frequency":3.98},{"id":9855,"text":"Align machines, cutterheads, or depth gauge makers with reference stakes and guidelines or ground or position equipment, following hand signals of other workers.","core":true,"importance":4.48,"relevance":67.8,"frequency":null},{"id":9868,"text":"Signal operators to guide movement of tractor-drawn machines.","core":true,"importance":4.4,"relevance":68.82,"frequency":3.8},{"id":9860,"text":"Repair and maintain equipment, making emergency adjustments or assisting with major repairs as necessary.","core":true,"importance":4.39,"relevance":80.02,"frequency":4.45},{"id":9856,"text":"Load and move dirt, rocks, equipment, or other materials, using trucks, crawler tractors, power cranes, shovels, graders, or related equipment.","core":true,"importance":4.33,"relevance":92.7,"frequency":5.57},{"id":9857,"text":"Drive and maneuver equipment equipped with blades in successive passes over working areas to remove topsoil, vegetation, or rocks or to distribute and level earth or terrain.","core":true,"importance":4.29,"relevance":98.86,"frequency":5.56},{"id":9859,"text":"Operate tractors or bulldozers to perform such tasks as clearing land, mixing sludge, trimming backfills, or building roadways or parking lots.","core":true,"importance":4.28,"relevance":93.57,"frequency":4.63},{"id":9867,"text":"Talk to clients and study instructions, plans, or diagrams to establish work requirements.","core":false,"importance":4.23,"relevance":55.44,"frequency":4.67},{"id":9854,"text":"Monitor operations to ensure that health and safety standards are met.","core":true,"importance":4.2,"relevance":84.68,"frequency":4.67},{"id":9862,"text":"Connect hydraulic hoses, belts, mechanical linkages, or power takeoff shafts to tractors.","core":true,"importance":4.11,"relevance":68.56,"frequency":3.72},{"id":9864,"text":"Select and fasten bulldozer blades or other attachments to tractors, using hitches.","core":true,"importance":4.1,"relevance":70.01,"frequency":3.46},{"id":9863,"text":"Operate loaders to pull out stumps, rip asphalt or concrete, rough-grade properties, bury refuse, or perform general cleanup.","core":true,"importance":3.98,"relevance":91.43,"